# BUILD A COMPLETE FULL-STACK APPLICATION: EMERGENCY FUEL ASSISTANCE SYSTEM

## 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Build a complete, responsive, full-stack web application named **FuelRescue — Emergency Fuel Assistance for Stranded Vehicles**.

The application helps drivers stranded on Indian highways because of insufficient fuel request emergency fuel assistance, share their exact location, identify suitable fuel sources or support providers, track request status, and complete assistance transactions.

The application must work offline for essential request creation and local record access. When internet connectivity returns, pending requests must synchronize with the backend server automatically and safely.

**15-second product explanation:**
“Stranded without fuel? Request emergency assistance, find suitable nearby fuel support, and track delivery—even offline. Your request syncs automatically when connectivity returns.”

Use the attached project document, *PSE_Modules_1_2_3_Filled_Emergency_Fuel_Assistance.docx*, as the foundation for the system requirements. Preserve its problem definition, stakeholder needs, system boundaries, causal relationships, leverage point, and evidence-validation principles.

Do not build merely a landing page or static demonstration. Build the actual frontend, backend, database integration, authentication, offline persistence, synchronization workflow, dashboards, and operational features.

