## 11. TESTING AND ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The application is not complete until these workflows have been implemented and tested.

### Test A: Normal online request
A registered driver creates a request. The backend validates it, saves it in Aiven PostgreSQL, and returns a confirmed request ID and status.

### Test B: Offline request
The driver opens the previously cached application without internet, creates a request, and sees it saved locally with PENDING_SYNC. The request must survive an application restart.

### Test C: Automatic synchronization
After connectivity returns, the application retries the request. The backend stores it once, returns its server ID, and the frontend changes its state to SYNCED.

### Test D: Duplicate prevention
Submitting the same client_request_id repeatedly must not create duplicate assistance requests or payment records.

### Test E: Synchronization failure
A server or validation error must not silently delete the local request. Show the error, preserve the data, and provide an appropriate retry or correction action.

### Test F: Provider workflow
A provider receives a valid request, accepts it, and updates its status. The driver sees confirmed status updates.

### Test G: Authorization
A driver cannot access another driver's private requests. A provider cannot perform administrative actions. Unauthorized requests are rejected by the backend.

### Test H: QR identification
An authorized scan retrieves the appropriate vehicle reference without exposing private data to unauthorized users.

### Test I: Location failure
If GPS permission is denied or Google Maps services are unavailable, the user can enter a location manually and continue where feasible.

### Test J: Responsive interface
All essential screens work on common mobile, tablet, and desktop viewport sizes.

### Test K: Database integration
The backend connects to Aiven PostgreSQL using environment-based configuration and persists records correctly.

### Test L: Payment integrity
A simulated payment is clearly labelled as a simulation. Repeated requests cannot create duplicate charges.

Provide automated tests for the most critical cases and a manual end-to-end testing checklist.

